# The Ultimate Guide to Rhinoceros 3D Scripting Resources

**Compiled by Manus AI | April 2026**

---

Rhinoceros 3D (Rhino) and its visual programming environment, Grasshopper, offer extraordinary power through scripting and plugin development. Whether you are automating repetitive tasks, generating complex parametric geometries, building full-fledged commercial plugins, or integrating Rhino with cloud services, the ecosystem supports multiple languages — primarily **Python** (both IronPython 2.7 and CPython 3.x in Rhino 8), **C#/.NET**, **VBScript** (legacy RhinoScript), and even **F#** and **JavaScript** via rhino3dm.js.

This guide catalogs the most valuable resources available across the web, organized by category. Free resources are marked clearly; paid resources are noted where applicable. The guide covers official documentation, GitHub repositories, Python and C# libraries, video tutorials, online courses, books, PDFs, community forums, specialized platforms, and academic resources.

